# Project: Profile

Purpose:
  Define project operational context so AI can choose architecture,
  skills, and implementation strategies that fit the actual project.
  This file defines the schema only — concrete values belong to the
  instantiated project (bax ./instantiation.sdd).

Owns: project\profile.sdd
Schema:
  Stack:
    BE:    <backend framework / language>
    DB:    <database>
    FE:    <frontend framework>
    MD:    <mobile framework>
    DO:    <deployment / orchestration>

  Scale:
    DAU:   <number>
    MAU:   <number>
    QPS:   <number>

  Availability:
    SLA:   <percentage>

  Architecture:
    <style: modular_monolith / microservices / serverless / ...>

  Regions:
    <count>

  Compliance:
    <standards: GDPR / SOC2 / ...>

  Constraints:
    <list>

  Goals:
    <list>

  ComplexityBudget:
    <L0-L5 scale constraint that gates which patterns are eligible>

  NFR:
    Latency:     <target>
    Availability: <target>
    Security:     <baseline>
    Recovery:     <RPO/RTO>

  SecurityRiskBudget:
    SecurityLevel:     <L0-L5>
    RiskTolerance:    <low/medium/high>
    CriticalAllowed:  <true/false>
    HighAllowed:      <true/false>
    PentestRequired:  <true/false>
    ExternalExposure: <public/internal/private>

NonGoals:
  A project instance MAY declare explicit non-goals to prevent AI from
  introducing scope creep via "best practice" additions the project has
  consciously excluded.

  Schema:
    NonGoals:
      <explicitly excluded concept>

  Examples (illustrative only):
    microservices, multi-region, blockchain, event-sourcing

Navigation:
  Schema: @schema.sdd
  Instantiation: @instantiation.sdd
  Architecture: @architecture.sdd

State: +
